// SPNs listed with setspn
//
// Fires when setspn runs a wildcard query, like "setspn -T corp.local -Q */*". That lists every
// account with an SPN, which is the target list for Kerberoasting. A query for one exact SPN
// is left out because admins use that to troubleshoot.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  Medium
// MITRE:     T1558.003, T1087.002
// Tables:    DeviceProcessEvents
// Custom details: AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName
//
// Needs:
//   - Nothing beyond Defender for Endpoint.
//
// Heads up: if you run Defender for Identity, its "Possible SPN enumeration via LDAP" alert
// can fire on the same activity.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check the account, the device and what launched it.
//   - Escalate if it isn't a known admin. Requesting tickets for those accounts is the next
//     step in a Kerberoast, so Tier 2 should check the domain controller logs.
//   - Close if it's ticketed admin work.
//
// Based on: Sigma "Potential SPN Enumeration Via Setspn.EXE".

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where FileName =~ "setspn.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName startswith "setspn.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine matches regex @'(?i)\s"*[-/]"*q"*(?:\s|$)'
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "*"
| project Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountDomain, AccountName, AccountSid, FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessParentFileName
